LANTERN REVISION 02 — EQUIPMENT, RESOURCES AND ALCHEMY

Five complete coherent revised packs, 52 logical assets. Current coverage is recorded by supersession_map.json. Every rebuilt master is a fresh built-in image_gen result with the canonical C/RUST source used only as an aesthetic reference. No bitmap editing cascades, recoloring, geometric transformations or alpha thresholding were applied to masters. Canonical hero and all original packs are unchanged.

ART DIRECTION
Authored variable-width contour, broad connected dark ink masses, intentional material-specific silhouettes, restrained earth/slate/ivory colors. Six-flat-tone prompt treatment was adopted after early metal candidates drifted toward textured render shading. Rejected candidates and early gate experiments are excluded from assets folders; they remain under rejected_candidates and style_gate for provenance only. The intentionally good salt pouch is retained from the old pack.

IMPORT LIMITATIONS
These are static conceptual cutouts, not rigged assets or exact physical-scale renders. Requested orthographic camera elevation 35.2643897 degrees and azimuth 45 degrees is a generated approximation, not a calibrated projection. No exact camera conformity is certified. Ground-drop conventions vary by subject and item recognition. Set world scale and pivot per item after runtime review; do not assume identical pixel occupancy is identical physical scale. Long shafts, strings and chain links require runtime checks at real display size.

ALPHA / PADDING
PNG masters preserve native RGBA. The alpha QA reports both all-nonzero bounds and visible bounds (alpha greater than 127). Some images contain isolated alpha=1/255 edge pixels, invisible on light/dark review composites. These are documented, not silently removed. Do not derive sprite tight bounds solely from any-nonzero alpha. Create standardized transparent padded import copies separately; use visible bounds for packing with at least 8-16 px atlas extrusion/padding as appropriate to target mip/filter settings. Do not include review-sheet backgrounds in game assets. Validate dark contours on actual game floors.

FILES
Each pack: assets/*.png native masters; assets/*.json exact prompt, source identity and generation provenance; pack_manifest.json ID map, hashes and alpha metrics; review_sheet.jpg includes 64 px light/dark proxies; before_after.jpg supports art decisions. Top-level supersession_map.json is the authoritative old-ID-to-current-art map. Source_map.json and jobs.json record original scope; use exact sidecars rather than jobs.json for final prompts when a fresh retry changed treatment.

REVIEW
Every image is visually checked in a large overview and light/dark gameplay-size proxy, with selected high-resolution originals inspected. These are art-review checks, not in-engine validation. Sources are not uploaded by this worker.
